   $q$Which explanation best shows how the word parts of "autograph" build its meaning in the last paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Auto means \"self\" and graph means \"chart,\" so it is a chart showing a person's own work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"},{"text":"Auto means \"self\" and graph means \"write,\" so it is a name written by the person herself.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Auto means \"car\" and graph means \"write,\" so it is writing printed on the side of a car.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"Auto means \"automatic\" and graph means \"write,\" so it is a name printed by a machine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Auto means "self" and graph means "write," so it is a name written by the person herself.$q$, $q$Auto means "self," so an autograph is a person's own handwritten signature, which is why Lucia "signed the woman's program." Car is a shortened word for automobile, not the meaning of the Greek root auto.$q$, 'draft', 'c2cf2ba2-64df-565a-8834-7b1373555e9f')
