  ('240e1692-eedc-59e8-85b8-37f1ebd99460', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How do the final two sentences, "We have the pool, the coaches, and the will. All we need now is your voice," help the author achieve her purpose?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By naming the coaches, they shift the focus to praising the staff rather than asking for anything.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"By listing what is already in place, they make family support seem like the only missing piece and urge readers to act.","is_correct":true},{"text":"By listing the school's resources, they show that the swim unit has already been approved by the board.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"By mentioning voices, they suggest that families should join a singing group to raise money for the pool.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By listing what is already in place, they make family support seem like the only missing piece and urge readers to act.$q$, $q$The list shows nothing is lacking except support, which turns the ending into a direct call to action. The proposal is still "going to the school board next month," so it has not been approved.$q$, 'draft', 'f573efa4-49a6-59e0-a30b-8a3e8ced985b')
