  ('2fb667fc-7c5e-537e-b5c1-f56426cd9066', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the final sentence, "the lesson it taught is still holding us up," support the author's purpose?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It suggests that the city is still delaying repairs because of what happened in 1974.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It plays on the idea of a bridge holding people up to suggest the lesson now supports the city's work.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It hints that the author worries the bridge may need to be replaced very soon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It reminds readers that the original steel plates are still in place under the newer coating.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It plays on the idea of a bridge holding people up to suggest the lesson now supports the city's work.$q$, $q$A bridge's job is to hold people up, so the phrase turns the physical image into a figure for how the lesson supports the city's practices. Nothing in the text says the bridge needs replacing.$q$, 'draft', '3a1704a8-3b51-5fe3-b2c2-e198b767e287')
