   $q$Why does the author mention "every eleven-year-old on a youth team"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To suggest that youth leagues should stop keeping any statistics at all","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"To show that what statistics count affects which skills young players choose to learn","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain that most youth players are too young to understand assists","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To point out that Raman began playing soccer at the age of eleven","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that what statistics count affects which skills young players choose to learn$q$, $q$She states that "Statistics shape what young players believe matters" and then gives the youth example as the consequence. She wants more statistics, not fewer, so the second choice reverses her point.$q$, 'draft', 'ed8d4aa5-ea67-5d94-b46e-4997ce84cee9')
