  ('fa0f649f-c33b-5334-a977-9f1b8d7a8792', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$At the end, Aunt Meera moves the tag rack beside her table and asks Priya to read tags aloud. What does this change suggest about how the two characters' relationship has developed?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Priya has proven she no longer needs supervision, so her aunt gives her more freedom.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Aunt Meera is embarrassed by her own handwriting and wants to hide the tags from customers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They will now work more closely, with Priya kept in the shop but guided by a new safeguard.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Aunt Meera no longer trusts Priya at all and plans to stop letting her work in the shop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstatement"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They will now work more closely, with Priya kept in the shop but guided by a new safeguard.$q$, $q$Moving the rack and adding the read-aloud rule keeps Priya working while building in a check, so the mistake leads to closer teamwork rather than punishment. Nothing suggests her aunt plans to send her away; she keeps giving her work.$q$, 'draft', '85aec348-c6e8-5c38-aaf7-533aef6db3a2')
