   $q$Lena simply points at her brother when their father asks who drove. Why does the speaker call this moment "everything"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because Lena takes all the credit for the harvest without mentioning him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Because her small, quiet gesture publicly confirms the respect he worked all week to earn.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Because it means he will never have to work on the farm again after that.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Because his father is angry that a younger child drove the tractor alone.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because her small, quiet gesture publicly confirms the respect he worked all week to earn.$q$, $q$Lena's point is brief ("That was all"), but it tells their father that her brother did the work, so it means "everything" to him. She points at him, so she is not taking the credit herself.$q$, 'draft', '1e97858a-fa63-5466-bfac-59a51c9825b3')
