-- Passage rg9-character-setting-plot-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('6ae20931-5b22-51dd-a9ce-24cadb34fd8a', 'rg9-character-setting-plot-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Frozen Screen$q$, $q$Mateo Villanueva signed up to volunteer at the public library because his school required twenty service hours, and the "Tech Help Tuesday" table seemed easier than shelving books. He pictured himself fixing passwords in thirty seconds and spending the rest of the hour on his phone.

His first visitor was Mr. Takahashi, a retired bus mechanic with a new tablet still wrapped in plastic. He wanted to make a video call to his granddaughter, Emi, who had moved overseas for university. He had tried twice at home. Both times the screen had frozen on his own startled face.

Mateo set up the account in five minutes and handed the tablet back. "Just tap the green button," he said.

Mr. Takahashi tapped the button. The call rang, connected, and froze. He tapped again, harder. Nothing. He set the tablet down very gently, the way a person sets down something he is afraid of breaking, and thanked Mateo for his time.

Mateo watched him reach for his coat. He thought about the clock on the wall and the twenty hours. Then he thought about how carefully the old man had laid the tablet down, as if the failure were his own.

"Wait," Mateo said. "Let's figure out why it freezes. It's probably not you."

They spent the next hour on it. The library's internet was fine; the problem was a setting that kept the camera in a power saving mode. Mateo found it, but instead of switching it himself, he talked Mr. Takahashi through each step and wrote them on an index card in large print.

At ten past four, Emi's face appeared on the screen, laughing, with a gray morning sky behind her. Mr. Takahashi did not speak for a moment.

The next Tuesday he came back with the index card and a friend from his old garage who also had a tablet. Mateo stayed an hour past his shift. He did not count it toward his hours.$q$, 'draft')
