  ('d44f790e-797c-5c39-8120-fee63c5bc72c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-comparing-texts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Text 1 states its lesson in its final sentence. How does Text 2 handle the same lesson?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It replaces the lesson with a different one about saving money for the future.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It has the boy's father explain the lesson to Dalia in a long speech.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It states the lesson in its opening sentence and then gives an example of it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It never states the lesson directly and lets Dalia's choice and its results show it.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It never states the lesson directly and lets Dalia's choice and its results show it.$q$, $q$Text 2 ends on the boy's grin rather than a moral, so readers infer the lesson from what happens. The father only shakes her hand, so the choice about a speech is not supported.$q$, 'draft', '6c3f7075-1d3b-539e-abd6-d3486257f75b')
