   $q$In Text 2, what does the speaker's viola part most closely correspond to in Text 1?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The carts that crossed the finished arch for a hundred years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-detail"},{"text":"The elders who shouted to each other across the water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-character"},{"text":"A single stone brought by one household to the bridge.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The cold stream that kept the two villages apart each spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A single stone brought by one household to the bridge.$q$, $q$The viola line is "thin and plain," just as one stone is too small alone, and both become part of a larger structure. The elders plan the bridge; they do not stand for one small contribution.$q$, 'draft', 'a103a213-ac53-5802-b32a-a4cabb12163f')
