   $q$The poem's last stanza mentions "a child" who can "find one stone." Why does the poet include this image?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To introduce a new character who will appear in a later part of the poem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To suggest that the concert hall was built from the stones of an old bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To link the speaker's feeling to the children in Text 1 who name their family's stone.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To show that the speaker is actually a child living in one of the two villages.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To link the speaker's feeling to the children in Text 1 who name their family's stone.$q$, $q$Text 1 ends with children naming "the stone their great-grandparents had given," and the poem compares hearing one's own part to that act. The image is a comparison, so reading the speaker as a real villager is too literal.$q$, 'draft', 'a103a213-ac53-5802-b32a-a4cabb12163f')
