   $q$Which statement best describes how Text 2 transforms the source tale?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It turns the tale's hopeful message into a warning that working together often fails in the end.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It keeps the tale's setting and characters but changes the ending so that the bridge finally collapses.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-plot"},{"text":"It moves the tale's physical bridge into music, so the shared structure is sound that lasts only one performance.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It removes the idea of contribution and focuses only on the beauty of the instruments themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It moves the tale's physical bridge into music, so the shared structure is sound that lasts only one performance.$q$, $q$The poem replaces stones with notes, and the flutes stand "on my sound" until "the final chord is done," a structure that does not last a hundred years. The poem keeps the hopeful message, so the choice about a warning reverses it.$q$, 'draft', 'a103a213-ac53-5802-b32a-a4cabb12163f')
