   $q$Why does the author of Text 2 most likely end with a line that echoes the faded note on page 41?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that the club's logbook is nearly full, so future members will have to start a new one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To show that Hiroshi is copying the earlier student's words because he has no ideas of his own.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show that every answer opens a new question, turning the legend's single blank corner into an ongoing cycle.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To show that Hiroshi failed, since he could not explain the star's pattern after a whole winter of work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that every answer opens a new question, turning the legend's single blank corner into an ongoing cycle.$q$, $q$Hiroshi found a nine-day pattern, then noticed "The pattern is not perfect," so his answer produces the next question. He succeeded in reporting his finding, so reading the ending as failure misses its hopeful tone.$q$, 'draft', '849e954b-34f1-59da-bde2-c7abf33fda03')
