   $q$Text 1 includes the line "Machines are fine servants, but a poor memory." How does Text 2 express this idea without stating it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kenji writes plain instructions after the crisis so that the knowledge is stored by people, not just the script.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The club decides to stop using computers and promises to do every future issue by hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The software update proves that newer machines always work better than older ones do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"Ms. Ostrova scolds Kenji for writing a script and tells him never to automate anything again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kenji writes plain instructions after the crisis so that the knowledge is stored by people, not just the script.$q$, $q$Adding "a page of plain instructions" shows Kenji learned the tool should not be the only place knowledge lives. Nothing says the club gives up the script, so that choice goes beyond the text.$q$, 'draft', '3b455230-0936-58e9-b7bb-34dc54865426')
