   $q$The final sentence mentions both "a shortage of firewood" and "a year of patient testing." What idea does pairing them suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Careful testing matters more than luck, so the accident was unimportant.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The firewood shortage alone was enough to change the village's future.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"An accident started the change, but careful work turned it into lasting success.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The village should plan for shortages of firewood in future winters.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An accident started the change, but careful work turned it into lasting success.$q$, $q$The accident produced the first green pots, but paragraphs 3 and 4 show it took a year of testing to make the color reliable. Each choice that keeps only one half leaves out the other.$q$, 'draft', '4f90803e-61d5-522f-b155-61b684912c27')
