   $q$In paragraph 4, the readings are "dispersed" to forecasting centers. Based on the context, "dispersed" means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"stored safely in a single location","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"checked carefully for mistakes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"sent out to many different places","is_correct":true},{"text":"changed into a different language","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$sent out to many different places$q$, $q$The sentence explains that the numbers are "not kept in one place" but are "spread out across a worldwide network," so dispersed means sent to many places. Stored in a single location is exactly what the text says does not happen.$q$, 'draft', '43f3d9bc-e288-5761-ae02-1de7bbc300fb')
