   $q$In paragraph 2, the pitcher gives the ball a fast "rotation." What does "rotation" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a throw that is very fast","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"a sudden drop toward the ground","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"a turning or spinning motion","is_correct":true},{"text":"a snap of the pitcher's wrist","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a turning or spinning motion$q$, $q$The text explains that the ball "turns over and over on its way to the plate," so rotation means spinning. The snap of the wrist is what causes the rotation, not the rotation itself.$q$, 'draft', '9e11bf80-ff75-501a-aecf-1443ffd0a4a5')
