   $q$In paragraph 3, the ball is "deflected." Based on the context, "deflected" means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"kept on a perfectly straight line","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"hit back toward the pitcher","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"pushed off its straight course","is_correct":true},{"text":"slowed down by thin air","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$pushed off its straight course$q$, $q$The word is restated as "turned away from the straight line it would otherwise follow." A perfectly straight line is what the ball would follow without spin, the opposite of being deflected.$q$, 'draft', '9e11bf80-ff75-501a-aecf-1443ffd0a4a5')
