   $q$The word "pronounced" can mean "spoken aloud." In paragraph 5, what does "more pronounced" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"harder for a batter to see","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"said more clearly by a coach","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"common-meaning-instead"},{"text":"slower to develop during flight","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"larger and easier to notice","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$larger and easier to notice$q$, $q$The paragraph contrasts a ball that drifts "an inch or two, which a batter can barely notice" with one that bends "more than a foot," so a more pronounced curve is bigger and more noticeable. The meaning "spoken aloud" does not fit a ball's path.$q$, 'draft', '9e11bf80-ff75-501a-aecf-1443ffd0a4a5')
