   $q$In paragraph 1, Hiroshi's hands are "jittery." What does "jittery" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"steady and relaxed","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"shaky from nervousness","is_correct":true},{"text":"tired from hard work","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"cold from the weather","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$shaky from nervousness$q$, $q$The next sentence says his hands "shook so much that he dropped his notes twice" before his first solo show, so jittery means shaky with nerves. Steady and relaxed is the opposite of hands that keep dropping things.$q$, 'draft', 'c66b1d7a-adef-5ba9-bbdd-e2e6140dc918')
