   $q$According to paragraph 3, what does the phrase "dead air" mean in radio?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a broken microphone in the booth","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"a song that listeners find boring","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"stale air inside a small, closed room","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"a period when nothing at all is being broadcast","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a period when nothing at all is being broadcast$q$, $q$The text defines dead air as "any stretch of silence when listeners hear nothing at all." Reading it as stale air in the booth takes the words literally and ignores the radio definition.$q$, 'draft', 'c66b1d7a-adef-5ba9-bbdd-e2e6140dc918')
